  body: |
    # Income other than earnings in the ESA source

    ## Authored interpretation

    The source describes different other-income scope for ESA(IR) and ESA(Cont), identifying specified exceptions to the general absence of an effect on ESA(Cont).

    ## Scope and boundaries

    DMG 51000 and 51003 distinguish this chapter’s other income from earnings. Gross treatment has specified exceptions, including differing recovery provisions; no assertion is made that all income or every deduction is treated alike.

    ## Inspected source passages

    - [DMG 51000, PDF page 2](https://assets.publishing.service.gov.uk/media/69a16f9cf534e7e99adaeaa5/dmg-ch-51.pdf#page=2)
    - [DMG 51003, PDF page 3](https://assets.publishing.service.gov.uk/media/69a16f9cf534e7e99adaeaa5/dmg-ch-51.pdf#page=3)
    - [DMG 51004, PDF page 3](https://assets.publishing.service.gov.uk/media/69a16f9cf534e7e99adaeaa5/dmg-ch-51.pdf#page=3)
    - [DMG 51006, PDF page 3](https://assets.publishing.service.gov.uk/media/69a16f9cf534e7e99adaeaa5/dmg-ch-51.pdf#page=3)

    ## Evidence and review status

    This is an unreviewed, model-assisted interpretation of selected passages in the frozen DWP guidance. It is an independent experimental publication, not an official DWP document, an entitlement decision or an executable benefits rule. ESA(Cont), ESA(IR), New Style ESA, UC and Pension Credit are not equated. The captured source contains historical, transitional and potentially superseded provisions; no complete or current legal rule set is claimed. Machine extraction can affect reading order, footnotes and characters. No visual PDF review or specialist acceptance is claimed.

